  "originalOptions": "A. Create a second ELB, and a new Auto Scaling Group assigned a new Launch Configuration with the new AMI. Use the Route53 Weighted Routing policy to adjust the proportion of traffic hitting the two ELBs.|B. Create new AMIs with the new app. Then use the new EC2 instances in half proportion to the older instances.|C. Redeploy with AWS Elastic Beanstalk and Elastic Beanstalk versions. Use Route 53 Weighted Round Robin Records to adjust the proportion of traffic hitting the two ELBs.|D. Create a full second stack of instances, cut the DNS over to the new stack of instances, and change the DNS back if a rollback is needed.",
